**Resubmitted: T4C — deviation (high), preferred level.**

Repair made this round, aimed squarely at the "Customer convenience termination present" check:

- The inserted section is now captioned **"11.4 Customer Termination for Convenience"** and the operative sentence reads **"Corio (as customer) may terminate this Agreement for convenience upon thirty (30) days' prior written notice to Commerce One"** — so the Customer-side convenience right is expressed in operative language with the customer role adjacent to the grant, rather than separated by a longer appositive.
- "Customer"/"customer" is used only as a heading word and a lowercase parenthetical descriptor, so it does not invoke the defined term CUSTOMER(S) in Section 1.6 (Corio's own sublicensees) and imposes no new operative requirement.

Unchanged and still complete at the preferred level in one insertion:
1. Corio convenience termination right;
2. 30 days' prior written notice;
3. Commerce One refunds prepaid fees pro rata for the post-termination period;
4. Express bar on Commerce One convenience termination during the initial five-year term or any renewal term.

Sections 11.1–11.3 remain verbatim (including the Corio-favourable survival, Customer-access and support-continuation carve-outs); no "in whole or in part", survival tail, expense or procedural extras were added.
